<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Deliberately empty.

  The app is not sandboxed, and nothing it does needs an entitlement:

    IOUSBHost      - a vendor-specific (0xFF) interface is claimed by no
                     kernel driver, so opening it exclusively needs no
                     entitlement and no root. Device *capture* would need
                     com.apple.vm.device-access, which GUD devices never
                     require.
    ScreenCaptureKit - gated by TCC (Screen Recording) at runtime, not by an
                     entitlement.
    CGVirtualDisplay - private CoreGraphics SPI; resolved at runtime.
    Sparkle        - needs extra entitlements only in sandboxed apps.

  Kept as a file so additions are explicit and reviewable, and so Release
  builds sign against a known-empty set rather than Xcode's injected
  defaults (which include get-task-allow and fail notarization).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
